    {
      "id": "Nc_5LUQ4lUklcDAqDvzSD",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1903.0404712071295,
      "y": 2576.028353599712,
      "width": 1920.2982177734375,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bNR",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 62025390,
      "version": 239,
      "versionNonce": 1465965685,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "LVnxUXpwY3FC1ClGl22aG",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1787919402637,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Re-validate the JWT (Defense in Depth):\n\nChecks the signature (using the cached IdP public key).\n\nExtracts tenant_id and clinician_id strictly for observability tags (logging), not for business logic.\n\nSchema Validation (Structure Check):\n\nEnsures the JSON payload is structurally sound (e.g., clinical_note.text exists and is a string).\n\nIf malformed, return 400 Bad Request. Do not pass go.\n\nProduce to Kafka (The Handoff):\n\nTakes the exact, raw JSON payload that the EMR sent, adds only two mandatory internal headers (trace_id and tenant_id), and publishes it to a single, unified Kafka topic (e.g., raw-ai-requests).\n\nReturns HTTP 202 Accepted with the tracking_id.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Re-validate the JWT (Defense in Depth):\n\nChecks the signature (using the cached IdP public key).\n\nExtracts tenant_id and clinician_id strictly for observability tags (logging), not for business logic.\n\nSchema Validation (Structure Check):\n\nEnsures the JSON payload is structurally sound (e.g., clinical_note.text exists and is a string).\n\nIf malformed, return 400 Bad Request. Do not pass go.\n\nProduce to Kafka (The Handoff):\n\nTakes the exact, raw JSON payload that the EMR sent, adds only two mandatory internal headers (trace_id and tenant_id), and publishes it to a single, unified Kafka topic (e.g., raw-ai-requests).\n\nReturns HTTP 202 Accepted with the tracking_id.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
